  "description": "Epsilla is an open-source vector database written in C++ that claims large speedups over standard HNSW by traversing its graph index in parallel, with support for metadata filtering, hybrid dense/sparse retrieval and a REST API, plus an embedded Python mode. Epsilla Inc. (YC-backed) has since shifted its business to an agent-as-a-service platform and no longer markets the database as a product. The repository still sees occasional commits, but there has been no tagged release since v0.3.16 in March 2025. Treat it as low-activity; choose Qdrant, Milvus or pgvector for new work.",
